#: ../../source/methods/preprocessing.rst:3
msgid ""
"Preprocess your data to remove noise and enhance the chemical information"
" contained in the spectra. Common preprocessing techniques include "
"baseline correction, smoothing, normalization, and derivative "
"transformations. These steps help eliminate unwanted variations caused by"
" instrumental drift or sample inconsistencies, allowing the model to "
"focus on the true chemical signals that drive accurate predictions."
